From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yi Xie <imxieyi@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 14 Sep 2026 10:33:54 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] kosmickrisp: advertise VK_KHR_shader_quad_control

The Android 17 Vulkan requirements profile (VP_ANDROID_17_requirements)
lists VK_KHR_shader_quad_control among its mandatory extensions, and both
Venus layers already carry it: the renderer allows it through
vkr_extension_table and the guest driver lists it as a passthrough
extension, so the host driver is the only layer that withholds it.

Everything the extension needs is already in place here. Its two
execution modes describe fragment behaviour Metal always has: fragments
are rasterized in 2x2 quads and the helper lanes of a partially covered
quad keep running, which is what RequireFullQuadsKHR asks for, and
derivatives are therefore quad-uniform as QuadDerivativesKHR requires.
The quad-scoped vote instructions the SPIR-V capability adds reach the
backend as nir_intrinsic_quad_vote_all and nir_intrinsic_quad_vote_any,
and the MSL backend already asks nir_lower_subgroups to rewrite both into
quad broadcasts. The Honeykrisp driver advertises the extension for the
same GPU family with no additional backend work.

Advertising the feature is also what enables the SPIR-V capability: the
common Vulkan runtime derives QuadControlKHR from shaderQuadControl.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/kosmickrisp/vulkan/kk_physical_device.c | 12 ++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 12 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/kosmickrisp/vulkan/kk_physical_device.c b/src/kosmickrisp/vulkan/kk_physical_device.c
index d9f4ceb20d7acb3bf7409fa7af6bac4e2ad409ef..f1b60389d7e004b57ccba4239532a6237ab04a8c 100644
--- a/src/kosmickrisp/vulkan/kk_physical_device.c
+++ b/src/kosmickrisp/vulkan/kk_physical_device.c
@@ -148,6 +148,7 @@ kk_get_device_extensions(const struct kk_instance *instance,
       .KHR_robustness2 = true,
       .KHR_shader_fma = true,
       .KHR_shader_maximal_reconvergence = true,
+      .KHR_shader_quad_control = true,
       .KHR_shader_relaxed_extended_instruction = true,
       .KHR_shader_subgroup_uniform_control_flow = true,
       .KHR_shader_untyped_pointers = true,
@@ -397,6 +398,17 @@ kk_get_device_features(
       /* VK_KHR_shader_maximal_reconvergence */
       .shaderMaximalReconvergence = true,
 
+      /* VK_KHR_shader_quad_control
+       *
+       * Metal rasterizes fragments in 2x2 quads and keeps the helper lanes of
+       * a partially covered quad running, so RequireFullQuadsKHR and
+       * QuadDerivativesKHR describe the behaviour this driver already has.
+       * The quad-scoped vote instructions the capability adds are lowered to
+       * quad broadcasts by nir_lower_subgroups, which the MSL backend already
+       * requests through lower_quad_vote.
+       */
+      .shaderQuadControl = true,
+
       /* VK_KHR_shader_relaxed_extended_instruction */
       .shaderRelaxedExtendedInstruction = true,
 
